All,

A Firefighter was struck and critically hurt this morning-assisting a motorist on
treacherous I-95 in Pennsylvania.

Firefighter Daniel Callaway was on his way to work at the Wilmington Manor Fire 
Company in New Castle County, Delaware, when he came upon a one car crash around
 04030 hours in the southbound lanes in Tinicum Township, Pennsylvania,

While helping the driver involved in the crash, Callaway was hit by a different 
vehicle and he was critically hurt. The 31-year-old was rushed to nearby Crozer 
Chester Medical Center and is reported to be unconscious.

FF Calloway also is affiliated with the Belvedere Fire Company in Newport, Delaware
and works as an EMT at Urgent Ambulance Services in Newark. Here is more: http://tinyurl.com/nrf3al3
[http://r20.rs6.net/tn.jsp?f=001JELdNQnWLkKu7RNbD1xd7MtWzuKWCit-rQMsR9Ssk9CT9FP0TYDZzSxpF3nHSQDO7NkYASFZca6pgOOJ2Th8ErKe4Rleh6CHiHa7oGy2MnKIGRB-7agZbMofKJGaowKYjhIj56sGwvqbkI3rbAXqR-X-4SFZees1sXKWMXBMOiHXDc4XDUavig==&c=u1tT-gT0NiUQ-BO4fo9B-HrjXtZ7mZRl3cVNyOzSGgHR8zSwZkXjwA==&ch=xjVO1sK8b__3IggmW2MH_Sr-nvjLTVni63ItXgIOQM9tfnIhuREYcQ==]

